      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"step-q53062\" class=\"step questionWidget\" stepid=\"q53062\" questionid=\"53062\" format=\"MC\" answer=\"\" current=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"><div class=\"questionWidget-header\"><div class=\"questionWidget-title\">Question 1</div><div class=\"questionWidget-helpButton\">?</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-text\"><p>Which of the following statements are true?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  A square is sometimes not a rectangle. </li><li>  A rectangle is always a quadrilateral. </li><li>  A square is never a rhombus. </li></ol></div><table class=\"questionWidget-choicesTable\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-53062-a\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">a</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">III only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-53062-b\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\" style=\"background: rgb(64, 64, 64); color: white;\">b</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">II only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-53062-c\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">c</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-53062-d\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">d</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">II and III only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-53062-e\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">e</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">None</td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-53062-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-53062-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>Let's now look at each statement in turn.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Statement I is false. In a rectangle, its four angles are right angles. The same is true for a square. A square is a specific type of rectangle, where the four angles are right angles and the four sides are congruent.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement II is true. A rectangle is always a quadrilateral because it has four sides.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement III is false. A rhombus is a parallelogram where all sides are congruent. A square is a specific type of rhombus, where the four angles are right angles and the four sides are congruent.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In conclusion, only statement II is true.</p>\n</div></div>",
